# cockpit/.env -- copy this file to .env and fill it in. .env is git-ignored;
# this example is tracked and holds NO values. One endpoint per role
# (cockpit/agent/llm.py), every one OpenAI-compatible:
#
#   planner   P   intent -> SPEC.md            a chat call
#   reviewer  H'  judges; if delegated, accepts a chat call
#   intent    I   goal -> node intents         a codex agent (an orchestrated run)
#   coder     C   SPEC -> code                 a codex agent (`cli.py code`)
#
# Per role: SGE_<ROLE>_BASE_URL, SGE_<ROLE>_API_KEY, SGE_<ROLE>_MODEL. Instead of
# the key itself, SGE_<ROLE>_KEYCHAIN=<service> reads it from the macOS keychain
# (security find-generic-password -s <service>), so it sits in no file at all.
# An unset URL or key falls back to the planner's; the planner's fall back to
# OpenRouter and OPENROUTER_API_KEY. A value already in the environment wins,
# so a run can override a role: SGE_CODER_MODEL=... uv run python cli.py run ROOT

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# P -- default: OpenRouter, z-ai/glm-5.2
SGE_PLANNER_BASE_URL=
SGE_PLANNER_API_KEY=
SGE_PLANNER_MODEL=z-ai/glm-5.2

# H' -- empty = the planner's (then H' reviews what its own model wrote)
SGE_REVIEWER_BASE_URL=
SGE_REVIEWER_API_KEY=
SGE_REVIEWER_MODEL=

# I -- no default model: an agent role must be chosen
SGE_INTENT_BASE_URL=
SGE_INTENT_API_KEY=
SGE_INTENT_MODEL=

# C -- setting SGE_CODER_MODEL makes `cli.py code` run C as a codex agent on this
# endpoint; without it, SGE_CODER_CMD is used (the cockpit's Codex button too).
# Example, DeepSeek with its key in the keychain as provider-switch.zsh keeps it:
#   SGE_CODER_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
#   SGE_CODER_KEYCHAIN=deepseek-api-key
#   SGE_CODER_MODEL=deepseek-flash
SGE_CODER_BASE_URL=
SGE_CODER_API_KEY=
SGE_CODER_MODEL=
SGE_CODER_CMD=codex exec
